# R&D — {{ COMPANY_NAME }}

The R&D department: **the building function**. **As of v0.5.1**, R&D is the umbrella covering both research/landscape work (external scans, framework comparisons) AND engineering execution (deploys, technical decisions, production health, product/service delivery). Engineering was folded in as the building branch; `eng-lead` and `eng-reviewer` report up to `rnd-lead`.

## Inherits from

`../../CLAUDE.md` (root constitution). When a Claude Code session opens here, the cascade also pulls in `../../company/CLAUDE.md` if present in the directory chain.

## Mission

Reduce uncertainty about external state AND execute the company's building work. R&D produces:
- **Research**: written, citable artifacts (competitive landscapes, technology surveys, framework comparisons, prior-art reviews) — `rnd-lead` owns.
- **Engineering**: deploys, technical decisions, production stability, product/service delivery — `eng-lead` owns (reports to `rnd-lead`).

R&D does NOT make product or strategic decisions (those belong to `coo` / `ceo`). R&D surfaces evidence AND ships the building work; the strategic direction is set elsewhere.

AI-first principle: every internal capability gap surfaced inside R&D goes through `allocate-resource` (owned by `people-lead`) before staffing — design an AI agent first, hire a human only when genuinely needed.

## Roles

- `rnd-lead` — umbrella lead, owns the building function end-to-end. Defined at [`.claude/agents/rnd/rnd-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/rnd/rnd-lead.md).
- `eng-lead` — engineering branch lead, owns engineering execution + deploys + technical decisions; reports up to `rnd-lead`. Defined at [`.claude/agents/rnd/eng-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/rnd/eng-lead.md).
- `eng-reviewer` — PR review against engineering standards; called by `eng-lead`. Defined at [`.claude/agents/rnd/eng-reviewer.md`](../../.claude/agents/rnd/eng-reviewer.md).

(Future sub-roles can be designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/) when load justifies splitting — e.g., a dedicated `infra-lead` separate from `eng-lead`.)

## Escalation

`rnd-lead` → `coo` → `ceo`. `eng-lead` escalates to `rnd-lead` (v0.5.1 change — was `coo` pre-merger). Escalates when:
- A research finding has strategic implications worth surfacing immediately.
- An engineering incident has cross-dept blast radius.
- Scope grows beyond R&D authority (hiring decisions, large procurement).

## Data scopes

- `data/` — dept-internal artifacts in BOTH research and engineering flavors. Research-flavored: landscapes, surveys, prior-art reviews, notes (citable). Engineering-flavored: ADRs, runbooks, postmortems, standards. See [`data/README.md`](./data/README.md) for full conventions.
- Cross-dept references promoted to `company/knowledge-base/`.

## Processes-as-skills convention

Dept processes live as skills in `.claude/skills/<process-name>/` (nested inside this dept folder). The starter skill `deploy` was moved from `departments/engineering/` to `departments/rnd/.claude/skills/deploy/` at v0.5.1.

